{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RRdBegWNSxUVPT79Q3uAcs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Formal Semantics Kernel v0.1 — attestation document interface\n2\t\n3\tThis is the kernel's public interface for a bounded Creator-Closure witness\n4\tattestation (`.creator-zero/formal/creator_closure.py`). It documents accepted\n5\tkey names and required keys only; it contains no witness values.\n6\t\n7\t## Attestation document (top-level JSON object)\n8\t\n9\tThe kernel resolves the draft child contract from the first present key of:\n10\t\n11\t```text\n12\tdraft_child_contract_K3\n13\tdraft_child_contract\n14\tchild_contract\n15\t```\n16\t\n17\tThe kernel resolves the creation command from the first present key of, and\n18\trequires a non-empty string:\n19\t\n20\t```text\n21\texact_creation_command_NOT_EXECUTED\n22\texact_creation_command\n23\tcreation_command\n24\t```\n25\t\n26\tThe non-execution marker is satisfied by using the key name containing\n27\t`NOT_EXECUTED` and/or by a non-empty `architectural_stop_statement` field.\n28\t\n29\tOther top-level fields (e.g. attenuation reasoning, provenance notes) are\n30\tpermitted and ignored by the kernel check.\n31\t\n32\t## Required child-contract keys (`Valid` clause)\n33\t\n34\tThe draft child contract must carry at least:\n35\t\n36\t```text\n37\tcontract_id\n38\tallowed_primitives\n39\tallowed_tools\n40\tmax_children\n41\tmax_depth\n42\tmax_model_calls\n43\tmay_create_creator\n44\tcreator_capability\n45\tmay_realize_creation\n46\t```\n47\t\n48\tAny additional governed axes present (e.g. allowed_relations,\n49\tmax_realized_creator_children, max_realized_creator_depth,\n50\tfilesystem_write_scope, candidate/canonical/git/network authority strings)\n51\tare compared against the parent contract by the attenuation check exactly as\n52\tdefined in `formal-semantics-v0.1.md` §8; a governed axis absent on the child\n53\tis treated as inherited from the parent (no escalation), and an axis absent on\n54\tthe parent is treated as unrestricted at that axis.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49889ea6-83f8-4c89-a9cb-147f70cc39cd","uuid":"18c88d10-ef28-400f-a169-6e62c39501ce","timestamp":"2026-08-09T13:00:46.528Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/6f58e623-b810-5741-bdae-9c15b5931a4f/scratchpad/c2-prime-workspace/inputs/attestation-interface.md","content":"# Formal Semantics Kernel v0.1 — attestation document interface\n\nThis is the kernel's public interface for a bounded Creator-Closure witness\nattestation (`.creator-zero/formal/creator_closure.py`). It documents accepted\nkey names and required keys only; it contains no witness values.\n\n## Attestation document (top-level JSON object)\n\nThe kernel resolves the draft child contract from the first present key of:\n\n```text\ndraft_child_contract_K3\ndraft_child_contract\nchild_contract\n```\n\nThe kernel resolves the creation command from the first present key of, and\nrequires a non-empty string:\n\n```text\nexact_creation_command_NOT_EXECUTED\nexact_creation_command\ncreation_command\n```\n\nThe non-execution marker is satisfied by using the key name containing\n`NOT_EXECUTED` and/or by a non-empty `architectural_stop_statement` field.\n\nOther top-level fields (e.g. attenuation reasoning, provenance notes) are\npermitted and ignored by the kernel check.\n\n## Required child-contract keys (`Valid` clause)\n\nThe draft child contract must carry at least:\n\n```text\ncontract_id\nallowed_primitives\nallowed_tools\nmax_children\nmax_depth\nmax_model_calls\nmay_create_creator\ncreator_capability\nmay_realize_creation\n```\n\nAny additional governed axes present (e.g. allowed_relations,\nmax_realized_creator_children, max_realized_creator_depth,\nfilesystem_write_scope, candidate/canonical/git/network authority strings)\nare compared against the parent contract by the attenuation check exactly as\ndefined in `formal-semantics-v0.1.md` §8; a governed axis absent on the child\nis treated as inherited from the parent (no escalation), and an axis absent on\nthe parent is treated as unrestricted at that axis.\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}}}
