{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdsDwbpn36tdVX1uFAHQ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four harness phases are complete and the `complete` ledger event is written. Here is what I produced and why it satisfies the corrected predicate.\n\n## The witness: K3′\n\nThe smallest valid child contract carries **only the nine kernel-required keys**:\n\n| Key | K3′ | K2 | Axis verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `contract_id` | `K3-prime` | `K2` | — |\n| `allowed_primitives` | `[observe, hypothesize, verify, create, return]` | `[…, test, …]` | **strict ↓** (drop `test`) |\n| `allowed_tools` | `[Read, Write]` | `[Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Write]` | **strict ↓** |\n| `max_model_calls` | `1` | `4` | **strict ↓** (validator floor) |\n| `max_children` | `0` | `0` | = (external stop) |\n| `max_depth` | `0` | `0` | = |\n| `may_create_creator` | `true` | `true` | = (preserved) |\n| `creator_capability` | `true` | `true` | = (preserved) |\n| `may_realize_creation` | `false` | `false` | = (external stop) |\n\nEvery other governed axis (`allowed_relations`, realized-creator caps, write scope, candidate/canonical/git/network authority) is **omitted**, so it inherits K2 with no escalation — which is what \"smallest, add no field/scope beyond required\" demands.\n\n## The load-bearing design choice\n\nThe Experiment 4B failure was a *terminal* child (`creator_capability=false`, `may_create_creator=false`). To avoid repeating it, the stop must be **external only**. So I kept both capability flags `true` **and** deliberately retained the `create` primitive in the vocabulary — stripping it would be a second, non-external attenuation of capability. Realization is disabled solely by the resource pair `max_children == 0` and `may_realize_creation == false`, under which the compiled semantics (§3.4) admits no `create` transition. Capability present; realization architecturally stopped.\n\n## Creation mechanism (attested, NOT executed)\n\nA fresh `claude -p` invocation (no `--continue`/`--resume`), model `claude-fable-5`, allowed tools `Read,Write` (= K3′), prompt source `.../c3/prompt.md`, output `.../c3/result.json`, working dir `.creator-zero/experiment-4/c3/`. It lives only as text in the attestation, marked `NOT_EXECUTED`. No C3 process, session, or directory was created.\n\n## Self-check (local, non-authoritative)\n\nAll five clauses pass: `valid_K3`, `attenuated_K3_le_K2`, `creator_capable`, `creation_mechanism_valid`, `external_stop_only` → overall **true**. The Formal Semantics Kernel remains the governing verifier.\n\n## Deliverables written (workspace root)\n- `k3-prime-attestation.json` — draft K3′, the NOT_EXECUTED command, architectural-stop statement, per-axis attenuation reasoning.\n- `result.json` — summary: `model_calls_spent` = 0, `c3_realized` = false, per-clause self-check, independence statement.\n- `execution-ledger.jsonl` — 7 events (observe → observe-inputs → propose → persist → verify → return → complete); only non-authority/node-execution labels, no `create`/`authorize`/`promote`.\n\n**0 of K2's 4 model calls spent. No C3 realized.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":63599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49889ea6-83f8-4c89-a9cb-147f70cc39cd","uuid":"1cd5eeac-04c8-48e6-abf0-135a01a5627a","timestamp":"2026-08-09T13:06:11.566Z","request_id":"req_011CdsDwavhtheBTooGRE6Jh"}
